## 3. Application Load Balancer (ALB)

### ALB Overview

ALB works at Layer 7 (Application Layer):
- Understands HTTP/HTTPS
- Reads HTTP headers (Host, Path, User-Agent)
- Makes intelligent routing decisions
- Perfect for microservices, containers, web apps

### Create ALB

```bash
# Create Application Load Balancer
ALB=$(aws elbv2 create-load-balancer \
  --name my-app-alb \
  --subnets subnet-public-1a subnet-public-1b \
  --security-groups sg-12345678 \
  --scheme internet-facing \
  --type application \
  --ip-address-type ipv4 \
  --tags Key=Name,Value=app-alb Key=Environment,Value=prod \
  --query 'LoadBalancers[0].LoadBalancerArn' \
  --output text)

echo "ALB ARN: $ALB"

# Create Target Group
TG=$(aws elbv2 create-target-group \
  --name web-targets \
  --protocol HTTP \
  --port 80 \
  --vpc-id vpc-12345678 \
  --target-type instance \
  --health-check-path / \
  --health-check-interval-seconds 30 \
  --healthy-threshold-count 2 \
  --unhealthy-threshold-count 2 \
  --matcher HttpCode=200 \
  --query 'TargetGroups[0].TargetGroupArn' \
  --output text)

# Register Targets
aws elbv2 register-targets \
  --target-group-arn $TG \
  --targets Id=i-0123456789abcdef0 Id=i-0123456789abcdef1

# Create Listener
LISTENER=$(aws elbv2 create-listener \
  --load-balancer-arn $ALB \
  --protocol HTTP \
  --port 80 \
  --default-actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$TG \
  --query 'Listeners[0].ListenerArn' \
  --output text)

# Get ALB DNS
DNS=$(aws elbv2 describe-load-balancers \
  --load-balancer-arns $ALB \
  --query 'LoadBalancers[0].DNSName' \
  --output text)

echo "Access at: http://$DNS"
```

### ALB Routing Rules

```bash
# Path-based Routing
aws elbv2 create-rule \
  --listener-arn $LISTENER \
  --conditions Field=path-pattern,Values=/api/* \
  --priority 1 \
  --actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$API_TG

# Host-based Routing
aws elbv2 create-rule \
  --listener-arn $LISTENER \
  --conditions Field=host-header,Values=api.example.com \
  --priority 2 \
  --actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$API_TG

# Method-based Routing
aws elbv2 create-rule \
  --listener-arn $LISTENER \
  --conditions Field=http-request-method,Values=POST \
  --priority 3 \
  --actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$API_TG
```

### ALB Features

- **SSL/TLS Termination** - ALB terminates SSL, communicates with backends over HTTP
- **HTTP/2 Support** - Automatically supported with ALB
- **WebSocket Support** - ALB maintains long-lived connections
- **Sticky Sessions** - Session affinity based on duration
- **Request Headers** - Adds X-Forwarded-* headers for client info

