## 5. Classic Load Balancer (CLB)

### CLB Overview

CLB (Legacy - Still Used):
- Layer 4/7 hybrid (understands some Layer 7, mainly Layer 4)
- Previous generation load balancer
- Still supported but ALB/NLB recommended
- Good for: Legacy applications, simple setups

### Create CLB

```bash
# Create Classic Load Balancer
CLB=$(aws elb create-load-balancer \
  --load-balancer-name my-classic-lb \
  --listeners Protocol=HTTP,LoadBalancerPort=80,InstancePort=80,InstanceProtocol=HTTP \
  --availability-zones us-east-1a us-east-1b \
  --query 'DNSName' \
  --output text)

# Register EC2 instances
aws elb register-instances-with-load-balancer \
  --load-balancer-name my-classic-lb \
  --instances i-12345678 i-87654321 i-11223344

# Configure Health Check
aws elb configure-health-check \
  --load-balancer-name my-classic-lb \
  --health-check Target=HTTP:80/health,Interval=30,Timeout=5,HealthyThreshold=2,UnhealthyThreshold=2
```

