## 6. Health Checks

### Health Check Configuration

```bash
# ALB Health Check
aws elbv2 modify-target-group \
  --target-group-arn $TG \
  --health-check-protocol HTTP \
  --health-check-path /health \
  --health-check-interval-seconds 30 \
  --health-check-timeout-seconds 5 \
  --healthy-threshold-count 2 \
  --unhealthy-threshold-count 2 \
  --matcher HttpCode=200,201,202
```

### Custom Health Check Endpoint

```bash
# Example health check endpoint (Node.js)
app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  // Check database connection
  if (!db.isConnected()) {
    return res.status(503).json({ status: 'unhealthy' });
  }
  
  // Check memory usage
  const memUsage = process.memoryUsage();
  if (memUsage.heapUsed > memUsage.heapTotal * 0.9) {
    return res.status(503).json({ status: 'unhealthy' });
  }
  
  // All checks passed
  res.status(200).json({ status: 'healthy' });
});
```

### Health Check Flow

```
Timeline: Health check every 30 seconds

Time │ Check Result │ Status
─────┼──────────────┼──────────────────────
0s   │ -            │ InService (initial)
30s  │ Failed (500) │ InService (wait for 2)
60s  │ Failed (500) │ OutOfService (2 failed)
90s  │ Success (200)│ OutOfService (wait for 2)
120s │ Success (200)│ InService (2 healthy)
```

