## 8. Listeners and Rules

### Create Listeners

```bash
# HTTP Listener (port 80)
LISTENER_HTTP=$(aws elbv2 create-listener \
  --load-balancer-arn $ALB \
  --protocol HTTP \
  --port 80 \
  --default-actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$TG \
  --query 'Listeners[0].ListenerArn' \
  --output text)

# HTTPS Listener (port 443)
LISTENER_HTTPS=$(aws elbv2 create-listener \
  --load-balancer-arn $ALB \
  --protocol HTTPS \
  --port 443 \
  --certificates CertificateArn=$CERT_ARN \
  --default-actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$TG \
  --query 'Listeners[0].ListenerArn' \
  --output text)

# Redirect HTTP to HTTPS
aws elbv2 create-listener \
  --load-balancer-arn $ALB \
  --protocol HTTP \
  --port 80 \
  --default-actions Type=redirect,RedirectConfig={Protocol=HTTPS,Port=443,StatusCode=HTTP_301}
```

### Listener Rules (Priority-based Routing)

```bash
# Rule 1: Priority 1 - API requests
aws elbv2 create-rule \
  --listener-arn $LISTENER_HTTPS \
  --priority 1 \
  --conditions Field=path-pattern,Values=/api/* \
  --actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$API_TG

# Rule 2: Priority 2 - Admin requests
aws elbv2 create-rule \
  --listener-arn $LISTENER_HTTPS \
  --priority 2 \
  --conditions Field=path-pattern,Values=/admin/* \
  --actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$ADMIN_TG

# Rule 3: Priority 3 - Static content
aws elbv2 create-rule \
  --listener-arn $LISTENER_HTTPS \
  --priority 3 \
  --conditions Field=path-pattern,Values=/static/* \
  --actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=$STATIC_TG
```

